From: Kyle Crenshaw <b1nc0d3x@gmail.com>
To: freebsd-wireless@freebsd.org
Cc: Adrian Chadd <adrian@FreeBSD.org>
Subject: [PATCH] net80211: minimal IGTK slot support for 802.11w MFP,
	aligned with D45887 / D46505 / D46668

Hi Adrian, hi list,

I hit the concrete instance of net80211's 802.11w gap while writing
a native FreeBSD driver for the Broadcom BCM43602 PCIe wifi chip
(brcm_pci, out-of-tree at github.com/b1nc0d3x/brcm-driver; 43602 is
the last consumer BCM4 part with usable brcmfmac fw v7.35.177.61).

The 43602 is FullMAC and the firmware does BIP-CMAC-128 integrity
checking internally, so end-to-end MFP would work if net80211 could
just route the IGTK from wpa_supplicant to the driver's iv_key_set
hook.  It can't today: ieee80211_ioctl_setkey rejects any kid >=
IEEE80211_WEP_NKID (4) at line 1206 with EINVAL, wpa_supplicant
gives up with "Failed to configure IGTK to the driver," and the
GROUP_HANDSHAKE tears the association down with reason 1.

Before writing this I searched the review queue and found your three
in-flight patches on exactly this area:

  D45887 - net80211: add a placeholder check routine for whether a
           key is an IGTK key                                     WIP
  D46505 - net80211: add MMIC element ID (for management frame
           protected group action frames)                        WIP
  D46668 - net80211: add initial support for extending the global
           key array to include IGTK keys                        WIP

D46668 in particular is the same shape.  I've kept the naming
(IEEE80211_MAX_NKID is the sum, ieee80211_is_key_igtk gets its
D45887-shaped signature) so review of this patch is really review of
the minimal subset of D46668 with the driver diffs (ath, rtwn)
stripped out.

Since your July 2025 note said "slowly working on it, it requires a
lot of cleanup in net80211" and the three reviews are tagged WIP with
D46668's commit message asking reviewers to hold off until you
rewrite it, I don't want to front-run your larger key-flags cleanup.
Two ways this could land:

  1. You take this as the mechanical subset of D46668 that unblocks
     FullMAC MFP now, and continue the driver-side auditing (ath,
     rtwn), the MMIC-IE work (D46505), and the ieee80211_is_key_igtk
     placeholder plumbing (D45887) at whatever pace the bigger
     refactor allows.  This patch is designed to compose cleanly with
     all three: same names, no overlapping fields.

  2. You'd rather this wait for your full stack to land as a single
     coherent series.  In that case just say the word and I'll keep
     the patch out-of-tree in the brcm_pci docs/patches directory.

What this patch touches, deliberately narrow:

  - IEEE80211_IGTK_NKID (2), IEEE80211_IGTK_KID_BASE (4),
    IEEE80211_MAX_NKID (6), and IEEE80211_KEY_IS_IGTK(kid).
  - iv_nw_keys[] grows from WEP_NKID to MAX_NKID slots.  All the
    existing pointer arithmetic against &vap->iv_nw_keys[0] stays
    valid, no UB.
  - Bound checks in setkey / getkey / delkey / delglobalkeys /
    is_key_global / crypto_resetkey init / ddb dumper / resume-time
    reinstall move from WEP_NKID to MAX_NKID.
  - IEEE80211_IOC_WEPKEY, IEEE80211_IOC_WEPTXKEY, and
    IEEE80211_IOC_NUMWEPKEYS stay at WEP_NKID; those paths carry
    WEP semantics and slots 4/5 are not WEP.

What this patch does NOT touch, yours to design:

  - Software wlan_bip_cmac cipher module.  Only needed for softmac
    drivers doing BIP in-host; FullMAC + fw-side BIP works without it.
  - The MMIC element ID handling from D46505.
  - Driver-side auditing (ath, rtwn key allocators skipping IGTK):
    each maintainer's call once the ABI change lands.
  - IGTK rekey / IPN replay counter validation semantics.
  - The wpa_supplicant driver_bsd shim.  My initial cover letter said
    it needed a dedicated IEEE80211_C_ PSK-SHA256 capability bit, but
    the AKM selection in wpa_supplicant.c:1876 comes out of ie.key_mgmt
    & ssid->key_mgmt (AP beacon intersected with the network block),
    not capa.key_mgmt, and MFP gating in wpas_get_ssid_pmf is on
    drv_enc & WPA_DRIVER_CAPA_ENC_BIP which unpatched driver_bsd
    already sets from IEEE80211_CRYPTO_BIP_CMAC_128.  Once the driver
    advertises BIP-CMAC-128 in ic_cryptocaps and the wpa_supplicant
    network block lists WPA-PSK-SHA256 in key_mgmt, MFP works with no
    shim change.

ABI note.  sizeof(struct ieee80211_key) is 216 bytes on LP64, so
iv_nw_keys[] grows by 432 bytes and struct ieee80211vap grows by
432 bytes.  Modules that embed a full ieee80211vap must be rebuilt;
ones that only carry a pointer are unaffected.  D46668 makes the
same tradeoff.

Testing on fbsdmac (MBP11,4, BCM43602 + fw v7.35.177.61) against
Ubuntu hostapd v2.10 with `ieee80211w=1`,
`wpa_key_mgmt=WPA-PSK WPA-PSK-SHA256`, `group_mgmt_cipher=AES-128-CMAC`:

  wpa_state=COMPLETED at t=2 s from wpa_supplicant start
  key_mgmt=WPA2-PSK-SHA256, pmf=1
  DHCPACK from 10.99.0.1, bound 10.99.0.17
  3/3 pings, 1.5-8.7 ms
  brcm_pci0: wsec_key: idx=4 len=16 algo=4 flags=0x0 peer=00...
  brcm_pci0: fmop_set_key: IGTK idx=4 algo=4 rc=0

5/5 rapid `ifconfig wlan0 down/up` + `pkill wpa_supplicant` + restart
cycles all complete in 3-4 s each, MFP renegotiated + IGTK
re-installed on every cycle.  No panics, no wedges.

One live-fire caveat that isn't fixed by this patch and doesn't
belong in it, but is worth flagging: on BCM43602, the fw's beacon
parser auto-expands the parsed RSN IE with an implicit PMKID+
group_mgmt suffix when MFPC is set in RSN caps.  Cached beacon IE
ends up 32 bytes; M3 arrives verbatim from hostapd at 26 bytes;
wpa_supplicant's byte-exact wpa_compare_rsn_ie fires
WLAN_REASON_IE_IN_4WAY_DIFFERS locally-generated right after
receiving IGTK material.  A tiny wpa_supplicant fallback that
accepts the mismatch when the parsed fields agree closes the loop --
posting that separately.  Without it, IGTK arrives at
ieee80211_ioctl_setkey but wpa_supplicant tears the assoc down at
step 3/4 and never fires the SIOCS80211 WPAKEY that this patch
exists to accept.

Full driver context: https://github.com/b1nc0d3x/brcm-driver.git
Companion wpa_supplicant patch:
  docs/patches/wpa_supplicant-semantic-rsn-ie-compare.diff

Happy to iterate on the shape.  Thanks for the ongoing net80211 work.

Cheers,
